# Code owners — reviewers GitHub requests automatically, and (with
# `require_code_owner_review` on the `main-required-gates` ruleset) the only
# reviewers whose approval satisfies the gate for these paths.
#
# Scoped deliberately rather than claiming the whole tree. The point is to make
# the paths where a malicious or careless change does the most damage impossible
# to land without an owner looking: the CI definition itself, the gates that
# decide what "green" means, the dependency pins, and the authentication
# boundary. A `*` catch-all would mean every typo fix needs the same ceremony,
# which is how CODEOWNERS files end up being bypassed instead of followed.
#
# Order matters: later patterns win, so the specific blocks come after the
# general ones.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CI, gates and release machinery
#
# A change here can turn every other control off. `codeql_sarif_gate.py` and
# `run_all_gates.sh` decide what passes; `codeql_baselines/` decides what is
# already-accepted debt, and a silent refresh there launders new findings into
# it. `codeql.yml` carries CODEQL_ACTION_DIFF_INFORMED_QUERIES, without which
# pull-request analysis stops seeing whole classes of regression.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
